Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.53,0:00:05.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Was it Your Grace who sent \NScarlett to the scaffold?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.32,0:00:08.37,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,What makes you think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.82,0:00:12.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The conclusive evidence\N in Cecilia's attempted assassination
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.20,0:00:16.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,was the bottle of poison \Nfound in Scarlett's chambers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.45,0:00:21.66,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Someone snuck through a duke's house\N and planted that in his daughter's room.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.68,0:00:25.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Only one person could do that \Nwithout leaving a trace,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.22,0:00:28.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and that person is you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.24,0:00:33.89,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You arranged Scarlett's execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.67,0:02:09.47,Main - Top + Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,Strangely, he and I came\N into the world on the same day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.16,0:02:14.67,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm so capable that \NI surprise even myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.30,0:02:18.77,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,but I still wish to serve you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.77,0:02:20.73,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,So take pride, Ern.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.17,0:02:24.19,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Dolphy, you can't be serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.58,0:02:28.25,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Remarry? Me?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.65,0:02:31.75,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,The Republic of Soldita is begging me
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.75,0:02:35.53,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,to take a descendant \Nof Cornelia Faris off their hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.92,0:02:41.89,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,I can't trust a lineage that dangerous \Nto just any noble house.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.30,0:02:46.51,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,So, well, you're my only real option.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.18,0:02:50.45,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Honestly... The things I do for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.55,0:02:58.89,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,I am Aliénore Shibola.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.66,0:03:04.57,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,My bride from across the sea \Nwas the very picture of a good wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.90,0:03:12.56,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,Her singular shortcoming\N was her frail constitution.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.27,0:03:18.33,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,However, it wasn't long\N before we had Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.99,0:03:21.11,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,I couldn't help it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.16,0:03:24.42,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,It was out of my hands, I tell you!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.42,0:03:26.43,Flashback,Dylan,0,0,0,,Coochie coochie coo.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.71,0:03:28.69,Flashback,Dylan,0,0,0,,What a beauty you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.17,0:03:31.68,Flashback,Dylan,0,0,0,,And you don't cry at the sight of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.93,0:03:35.79,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Dylan, don't hold her too long. \NWhat if your stupidity rubs off on her?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.79,0:03:37.19,Flashback,Dylan,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.19,0:03:41.07,Flashback,Dylan,0,0,0,,Did you hear that, sire?! \NWasn't that uncalled for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.07,0:03:44.71,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yes, I heard it, and I share his concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.71,0:03:47.28,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,You'd better hand \Ndear little Scarlett back to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.28,0:03:49.20,Flashback,Dylan,0,0,0,,What do I do? I'm surrounded by enemies!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.01,0:03:56.70,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,Looking back, those might \Nhave been the final days
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.70,0:03:59.81,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,we'd laugh together in blissful ignorance.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.91,0:04:05.49,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Word has it a strange hallucinogen \Nhas been circulating recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.49,0:04:06.59,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,A drug?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.01,0:04:10.79,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,It's chiefly popular \Namong young aristocrats,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.29,0:04:13.86,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,which makes me wonder \Nhow they're getting it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.86,0:04:17.07,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Only prominent nobles have the stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.74,0:04:20.61,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,And what is this hallucinogen called?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.61,0:04:22.74,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Jackal's Paradise.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.66,0:04:27.32,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,At the time, it seemed a trivial matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.72,0:04:31.15,Main - Italics,Adolphus {N},0,0,0,,But one day, some months later...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.71,0:04:34.42,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Dylan's been jailed for treason?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.68,0:04:39.43,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Yes. Given the circumstances,\N I doubt he can avoid the headsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.07,0:04:41.89,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,That's preposterous!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.89,0:04:44.17,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Naturally, Dylan would never turn traitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.71,0:04:47.16,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Someone framed him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.16,0:04:49.11,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,And their goal is...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.15,0:04:52.56,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,You don't mean... war?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.94,0:04:57.56,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,It's Faris. They've secretly \Nbeen pulling the strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.10,0:05:00.14,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,"The Holy Grail of Eris"?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.19,0:05:06.72,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Dylan is a pillar of our border defense. \NThey'll invade once he's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.20,0:05:11.22,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Then Dylan was sentenced \Nto death so quickly because...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.71,0:05:15.33,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Yes. We have rats in our midst.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.27,0:05:21.98,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Could Daeg Gallus be using \Nthe drug to secure funds?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.98,0:05:25.44,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Given its popularity \Nwith the upper nobility,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.44,0:05:28.96,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,they almost certainly mean \Nto erode our nation from within.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.96,0:05:33.51,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,And amid it all, \None man has seen a meteoric rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.97,0:05:36.97,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Simon Darkian!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.39,0:05:40.55,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Question him at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.55,0:05:43.59,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,He'd only plead ignorance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.05,0:05:45.78,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,We have no proof.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.78,0:05:47.74,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,What a disaster!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.63,0:05:56.07,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Is the poisoning accusation against \NScarlett part of their plan as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.40,0:05:59.02,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,No, that must be coincidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.02,0:06:02.08,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,They have no motive to harm Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.36,0:06:07.75,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,That's true... \NThey want her on the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.44,0:06:12.95,Flashback - Italics,Ernst {M},0,0,0,,That means without Scarlett, \Ntheir plan falls apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.95,0:06:14.31,Flashback - Italics,Ernst {M},0,0,0,,In which case...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.53,0:06:24.32,Flashback - Italics,Ernst {M},0,0,0,,What am I thinking?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.12,0:06:34.95,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Sire, I suggest we make use of Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.18,0:06:42.65,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Their plan requires a pawn possessing \Nthe blood of the old imperial family.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.24,0:06:48.27,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Executing Scarlett will buy us a way out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.27,0:06:54.22,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,It will stall them and sow the sentiment\Nthat public executions are barbaric.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.81,0:06:58.87,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,I'll task Kimberly Smith of the Violet \NAssociation with leading the outcry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.51,0:07:03.26,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,That will allow us \Nto delay Dylan's execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.26,0:07:04.98,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Wait, wait, wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.37,0:07:08.65,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,In the meantime, I will gather \Nproof of his innocence.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.65,0:07:10.24,Flashback,Ernst,0,0,0,,Wait, Dolphy!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.24,0:07:11.23,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.98,0:07:18.16,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Commit the face of every person \Nwho pleads for Scarlett's life to memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.82,0:07:22.99,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Their agents will be among them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.25,0:07:31.50,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,We'll show them all \Nthat we shall be the ones
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.37,0:07:35.23,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,who will have the last laugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.25,0:07:46.06,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Supposing that I did engineer \Nmy daughter's execution,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.52,0:07:49.15,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,what is that to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.34,0:07:51.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm doing this for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.49,0:07:53.63,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,"Her"?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.54,0:07:57.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,May I have your permission to speak?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.37,0:08:00.66,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.61,0:08:18.18,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,How are you feeling?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.49,0:08:23.43,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,If I didn't know any better,\N I'd think you were worried about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.43,0:08:27.37,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Of course I am. You're my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.95,0:08:31.75,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,Listen, dear...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.18,0:08:36.08,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,Don't give me that nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.32,0:08:42.30,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,A woman you don't sleep with and only \Nsee to exchange the occasional greeting
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.30,0:08:45.43,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,isn't what most people would call a wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.97,0:08:49.01,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,You're thinking of a mere acquaintance.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.56,0:08:53.46,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Are you angry?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.46,0:08:58.72,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,I'm only asking that you spare me \Nyour foolery, you dunderhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.01,0:09:00.41,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.41,0:09:04.86,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,Why, you can hardly expect \Na young lady to spell it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.24,0:09:08.99,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,I may be a silly little girl,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.45,0:09:13.85,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,yet even I know the blood\N in my veins could spark a fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.17,0:09:18.83,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,But do you expect me\N to just grin and bear it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.24,0:09:23.11,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,To just accept a life of \Nbeing treated like a prisoner?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.61,0:09:27.24,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,What is that but a living death?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.15,0:09:35.99,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,I think I'd like to be very selfish \Nand have some harsh words with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.99,0:09:37.18,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.67,0:09:50.29,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,I believe that when most people say \N"harsh words," they do mean {\i1}words{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.63,0:09:52.78,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,Oh, do forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.78,0:09:58.65,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,Back where I come from, \Nwe talk to dunderheads with our fists.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.65,0:10:01.66,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,What a lawless place that must be.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.66,0:10:06.02,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,I've done a lot of thinking \Nsince I came to this country,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.02,0:10:11.79,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,and I've decided to live my life\Nas I please after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.16,0:10:16.28,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,That {\i1}was{\i0} our dear Cornelia's dying wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.68,0:10:18.51,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,It was?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.51,0:10:20.68,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,Yes. And so...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.04,0:10:24.71,Flashback,Aliénore,0,0,0,,If you have a complaint, \Ntell it to Cornelia Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.60,0:10:31.68,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.68,0:10:33.93,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,I actually went and did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.75,0:10:37.06,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh, do forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.06,0:10:42.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,But my mother taught me to speak \Nto dunderheads with my fists.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.90,0:10:49.46,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Th-That was, um, a custom from\N the homeland of my friend's mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.91,0:10:51.39,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Your friend...?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.39,0:10:55.45,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, something about the best way \Nto deal with dunderheads.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.02,0:11:02.47,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, not that I mean to call \NYour Grace a dunderhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.89,0:11:06.70,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,What's a little slap?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.70,0:11:09.39,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,It hurt a lot worse back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.04,0:11:15.22,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,So, what else does your friend want?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.68,0:11:19.31,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Shall I offer my head, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.60,0:11:22.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,P-P-Perish the thought!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.11,0:11:23.47,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.47,0:11:26.61,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,If you ever have need of it,\N you need only ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.74,0:11:31.37,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Does Your Grace...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.47,0:11:34.19,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,wish to die?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.44,0:11:39.37,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Oh, that must be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.84,0:11:43.15,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,I've been longing for death, have I?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.63,0:11:51.35,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,I deserve to be punished. Otherwise...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.90,0:11:57.80,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,She'd be too pitiful for words, robbed \Nof her life through no fault of her own.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.55,0:12:02.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.55,0:12:11.28,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,If I may...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.62,0:12:18.04,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I have never once thought myself pitiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.18,0:12:24.05,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Yes, I felt anger and sadness as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.42,0:12:27.40,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,But I know how awkward \Nand proud you are, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.40,0:12:28.82,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,You couldn't help yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.13,0:12:34.11,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,And you've no reason to pity me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.78,0:12:36.70,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,After all, I know...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.87,0:12:40.81,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,that I came into this world loved.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.13,0:12:48.47,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Even I know that you loved me, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.29,0:13:05.11,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,There's plenty I'd like to say to you, \Nbut as for the rest of my complaints,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.93,0:13:10.22,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I suppose I'll just have to \Ntell them to Cornelia Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.19,0:13:14.62,Main - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.51,0:13:17.76,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,You must know what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.50,0:13:22.34,Main - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,Oh, I know. I know, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.31,0:13:26.80,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Mother was always saying it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.66,0:13:32.31,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Scarlett...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.18,0:13:37.18,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,I'll have your casket made of jet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.18,0:13:41.16,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,It's a sacred wood, said to guide souls \Nto the promised land.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.58,0:13:47.41,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,And I won't forget a blanket \Nwoven of moonworm cocoons.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.41,0:13:49.72,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,I can't have you getting a chill.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.28,0:13:53.77,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,Remember how often you caught colds \Nwhen you were little?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.77,0:13:57.29,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,You grew feverish so quickly,\NI couldn't take my eyes off you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.10,0:14:02.99,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,I know. Why don't I add \Nlovely engravings to your casket?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.57,0:14:07.54,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,You never would settle \Nfor less than the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.89,0:14:12.96,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,Really, you were always so willful and...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.56,0:14:23.50,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,Had there been any other way,\NI would've given anything for it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.07,0:14:28.38,Flashback - Italics,Adolphus {M},0,0,0,,I would have given my own life \Nmany times over!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.26,0:14:34.81,Flashback,Adolphus,0,0,0,,If only I'd told you even once \Nthat I loved you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.59,0:14:57.37,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Please, do your best for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.61,0:15:02.91,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Simon Darkian is with Daeg Gallus?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.41,0:15:07.12,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Cecilia recently purchased \Nthe Saint Nicholas Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.75,0:15:13.34,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,When Campbell owned it, tax inspectors \Ngave even blank books a pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.93,0:15:18.43,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,You don't mean Simon Darkian was \Nin charge of those inspections, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.43,0:15:20.20,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I mean just that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.62,0:15:24.80,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,A man named Edmond Park, \Nwho did the hospital's accounting,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.80,0:15:26.64,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,was found murdered.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.64,0:15:28.65,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,To silence him, most likely.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.30,0:15:31.69,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Meaning they kept secret books.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.69,0:15:36.07,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,We may be able to round up \Nthe whole gang if we can locate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.72,0:15:38.55,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,I entrust the matter to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.55,0:15:39.33,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.32,0:15:44.34,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,On that note... \NI heard Simon Ulster passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.25,0:15:48.64,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,My condolences. When is the funeral?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.47,0:15:52.02,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Today. Only for close family.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.85,0:15:55.09,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Will you be going alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.35,0:15:56.49,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Yes. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.60,0:16:03.34,Default,San,0,0,0,,I can't say much has changed on our end.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.71,0:16:08.67,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,SECOND PRINCE OF FARIS\NRODERICK
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.71,0:16:08.83,Default,San,0,0,0,,Second Prince Roderick is still \Navoiding public appearances.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.13,0:16:13.09,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,THIRD PRINCESS OF FARIS\NALEXANDRA
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.83,0:16:12.95,Default,San,0,0,0,,Third Princess Alexandra\N is still locked in the tower
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.95,0:16:14.63,Default,San,0,0,0,,and on track to be burned.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.01,0:16:22.98,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,FOURTH PRINCE OF FARIS\NTHEOPHILIS
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.02,0:16:20.21,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,And Fourth Prince Theophilis\N is already acting like he's king.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.21,0:16:24.37,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,I hear his followers have even\N picked a date for the coronation.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.69,0:16:28.15,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Then the one behind \Nthe Holy Grail of Eris must be...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.15,0:16:32.38,Default,San,0,0,0,,Indeed, Fourth Prince Theophilis \Nseems the obvious suspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.38,0:16:34.76,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Why, Connie!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.05,0:16:36.37,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Mylene.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.37,0:16:37.51,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Who are these ladies?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.31,0:16:41.51,Default,San,0,0,0,,We were just leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.74,0:16:45.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Mylene, how is your work?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.48,0:16:51.07,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,I'm writing articles to sell to the papers\N on my way to becoming a real reporter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.07,0:16:54.66,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,My latest is on the suspicious death \Nof Edmond Park.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.66,0:16:56.62,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Who's Edmond Park?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.99,0:17:00.60,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,The head of an accounting firm. \NHe was found murdered.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.60,0:17:03.54,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,It appears to have been\Na work-related vendetta.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.54,0:17:08.66,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,His clients included the Raven Trading \NCompany and Saint Nicholas Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.90,0:17:11.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Did she say Saint Nicholas Hospital?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.66,0:17:18.29,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Say, Mylene, isn't Saint Nicholas\N the hospital Earl Campbell used to run?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.29,0:17:20.60,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,I see you know all about it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.60,0:17:26.31,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Just between us, I hear Edmond Park \Nand Earl Campbell were gambling buddies.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.63,0:17:31.31,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,And it seems one gambling den \Nin particular was his favorite.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.31,0:17:36.33,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,It's under a restaurant called\N The Goat's Hoof.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.68,0:17:41.57,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are you waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.85,0:17:45.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How did I get myself into this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.05,0:17:47.48,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,What are you doing in a place like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.11,0:17:52.84,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Dear me. It's Kimberly Smith \Nof the Violet Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.36,0:17:54.97,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She's not wearing pink?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.72,0:18:02.04,Default,Waiter,0,0,0,,Your order?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.04,0:18:03.72,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Meat on the bone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.72,0:18:07.26,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,The kind where top and bottom \Nadd up to seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.34,0:18:10.31,Default,Waiter,0,0,0,,So {\i1}that's{\i0} what you're here for.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.31,0:18:12.86,Default,Waiter,0,0,0,,Sorry, downstairs isn't open yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.86,0:18:14.61,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Oh, what a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.61,0:18:18.86,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,But I'm only here to pick up\N something for Ed today.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.64,0:18:20.70,Default,Waiter,0,0,0,,This way.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.48,0:18:33.31,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I assume you're here \Nabout the Edmond Park case.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.31,0:18:35.00,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Who told you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.00,0:18:37.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A friend. She wants to be a reporter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.58,0:18:39.67,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,My. She has promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.09,0:18:43.92,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Aren't you engaged to Randolph Ulster?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.46,0:18:47.76,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Do you know who the Ulsters are?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.05,0:18:51.81,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,"Ulster" isn't merely a surname.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.81,0:18:56.29,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,It's also a title for agents who \Ndispose of the royal family's enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.29,0:18:58.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Agents?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.15,0:19:05.75,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Randolph serves in the military now, \Nbut the late Simon Ulster trained him,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.75,0:19:08.55,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,even though the duty \Nhas long since become a formality.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.06,0:19:14.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,E-Excuse me, but why tell me this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.04,0:19:17.34,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Good question. I also—
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.14,0:19:20.10,Default,Waiter,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.40,0:19:24.36,Default,Waiter,0,0,0,,This is it. Some kind of secret \Naccounting ledger, I hear.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.36,0:19:26.54,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Why, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.74,0:19:36.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Aren't those people...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.36,0:19:40.36,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,They really must not want us \Nreading that secret ledger.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.17,0:19:45.12,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Keep your eyes on me. \NPut it in your purse.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.86,0:19:49.91,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,This is all the help I can give you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.91,0:19:52.39,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Go out the back door. Hurry now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.39,0:19:54.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But what about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.10,0:19:58.78,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I don't need deadweight.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.78,0:20:02.38,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I was trained by Simon Ulster as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.39,0:20:12.05,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,He should be at Simon's funeral now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.14,0:20:15.12,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Take good care of Junior.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.13,0:20:32.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That's not what you should be doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.15,0:20:35.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.59,0:20:57.01,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Miss Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.80,0:20:59.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I saw it was raining.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.87,0:21:05.41,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What brings you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.41,0:21:10.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well, the thing is, \NKimberly left this in my care.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.86,0:21:18.23,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,How many times must I tell you\N not to act on your own?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.23,0:21:19.83,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.25,0:21:22.48,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But Your Lordship was alone too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.94,0:21:26.09,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So won't you call us even for today?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.84,0:21:31.61,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Don't I unnerve you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.16,0:21:33.34,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Pardon?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.65,0:21:37.48,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,My parents, my brother, \NLily, my granduncle...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.48,0:21:40.97,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,People close to me keep dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.61,0:21:46.21,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Don't you think I really am\N like Death himself?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.50,0:21:51.25,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your fiancée...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.90,0:21:56.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,lost her last betrothed to another woman,\Nmade a spectacle of herself at a ball,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.95,0:21:59.80,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,gets mixed up in one criminal \Nincident after another,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.61,0:22:04.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and, worst of all, she's haunted \Nby the wickedest woman of the age.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.44,0:22:07.56,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Doesn't that unnerve {\i1}you{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.80,0:22:14.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Let's leave together, Your Lordship.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.10,0:22:15.95,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.96,0:22:27.97,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(480,524)\fs12\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(180,290.666)}Translation:\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWilliam Varteresian
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.68,0:22:33.68,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(500,520)\fs10\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(160,255)}Subtitle Timing:\N{\fs12}Edgar Cruz\N\N\N{\fs10}Subtitle Editing:\N{\fs12}Riley Dalton
